{
  "id": "intune",
  "name": "Intune / Endpoint Manager delegation",
  "version": 2,
  "groupNamePattern": "PIM-{Role}",
  "_doc": "Only Intune RBAC roles (Graph deviceManagement/roleDefinitions) belong here -- the Intune binding can assign nothing else. Cloud PC Administrator / Reader (roleManagement/cloudPC), Windows Autopatch Administrator / Reader and Organizational Messages Manager live on OTHER RBAC surfaces: they are future workload connectors, not Intune rows. Shipping them here would create groups that can never be bound to their role -- orphan permission groups.",
  "description": "Permission groups for Microsoft Intune (Endpoint Manager). These are workload groups: Intune assigns its built-in RBAC roles directly to the Entra group (deviceAndAppManagementRoleAssignment) - no Entra directory role involved. Each group ships WITH its Intune role binding (a PIM-Assignments-Workloads row, connector 'intune'), so the group and its role are imported as one unit and no group is left without its role. Group names follow your own naming pattern. v1 shipped the classic six built-in roles; v2 moves every group to the workload data plane (WDP), sets the level ladder (managers and administrators L3, operators L4, readers L5), and adds Endpoint Privilege Manager, Endpoint Privilege Reader, Intune Role Administrator and Multi Admin Approval Policy Manager.",
  "rows": {
